### Byte Streams vs. Character Streams in Java

| Comparison Parameter | Byte Streams | Character Streams |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Data Unit** | Operates on **8-bit bytes** (binary data). | Operates on **16-bit Unicode characters** (text). |
| **Root Abstract Classes** | `InputStream` and `OutputStream` | `Reader` and `Writer` |
| **Standard Implementations** | `FileInputStream`, `FileOutputStream` | `FileReader`, `FileWriter` |
| **Primary Use Cases** | Images, audio, video, raw binary files, PDF. | Text files, source code, internationalized text (UTF-8). |

```java
// Reading with Byte Stream
FileInputStream in = new FileInputStream("image.png");
int byteData = in.read();

// Reading with Character Stream
FileReader reader = new FileReader("notes.txt");
int charData = reader.read();
```

$$\therefore \text{Character streams handle 16-bit Unicode internationalization automatically without encoding errors.}$$
